claimed: intent-tiebreak-by-example — what the precedence refusal suggested: render a tie-break as EXAMPLES of the disputed case rather than as prose. Prose cost 0.043 macro F1 and diluted every class; few-shot examples are the one lever that has paid consistently in this line. Two arms over the same 120 messages, differing only by two added examples: a message that both proposes a time and asks for an action, and a cancellation with no new time offered. Nothing in the library changes for the measurement, which is itself the point -- a tie-break carried as an example rides the channel that already works. If it pays, the Taxonomy[I] typeclass refused yesterday comes back EARNED, carrying examples rather than prose; if it does not, the honest conclusion is that this taxonomy overlap is not fixable from the prompt at all.
